course: dictionary
lesson: 3713
title: Fleshy and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Fleshy can mean thick, soft and juicy, or plump like a body part. It can also describe the pinkish colour of skin.
explain: «The cashew nut grows under a fleshy cashew apple.» Here fleshy describes a fruit that is soft and juicy. Ask: what word would fit here? Thick, soft and juicy fits, so that is the right meaning.
explain: «The coelacanth's fleshy fins move like legs.» Fins are body parts, so fleshy means thick and full of flesh here. Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Fleshy is an adjective, so it describes a noun: fleshy fruit, fleshy leaves, or the fleshy part of your thumb.
fact: «Fleshy» means thick, soft and juicy, like a plum or a tomato.
fact: «Fleshy» can also describe a body part that is plump, like «the fleshy part of your thumb».
fact: Fleshy leaves store water, which helps desert plants survive.
fact: Fleshy fruits like plums and tomatoes are eaten by animals, which then spread the seeds.
exercise: «The cashew nut grows under a fleshy cashew apple.» What does fleshy describe? | A metal tool | A sharp rock | A cold wind | *A soft, juicy fruit
exercise: «The star-nosed mole's star has 22 fleshy rays.» What does fleshy suggest about the rays? | Thin and see-through | Painted bright red | Made of wood | *Thick and full of flesh
exercise: Which of these is a fleshy fruit? | Spoon | *Tomato | Pebble | Paper
test: «The cashew nut grows under a fleshy cashew apple.» Which word in the sentence describes the apple? | Nut | Grows | Under | *Fleshy
test: «The fleshy part of your thumb» is which kind of part? | *Plump, full of flesh | Made of glass | Sour, like a lemon | Very fast
exam: Ella says fleshy means dry and crispy, like toast. Is she right? | Yes, like toast | Not sure, it is a made-up word | *No, fleshy means thick, soft and juicy | Yes, it means empty inside
